{"id":"547e48ef-f8e8-42fc-b2c1-fac0152115cb","object":"chat.completion","created":1793332296,"model":"deepseek-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"Now locate the exact wording for the remaining answers by extracting only keyword-bearing lines from the relevant pages (parsing the tool's `stdout` JSON, so output stays small).\n\n```python\nimport json, re\n\ndef grab(pages, kws, maxc=4000):\n    for p in pages:\n        r = read_pdf(p, p)\n        data = json.loads(r['stdout'])\n        txt = data['pages'][0]['text']\n        lines = [l.strip() for l in txt.split('\\n') if l.strip()]\n        for i, l in enumerate(lines):\n            if any(k.lower() in l.lower() for k in kws):\n                print(f\"[p{p}] {l[:maxc]}\")\n        print('---')\n\ngrab([4], ['categor', 'three', 'reason', 'act', 'interact'])\ngrab([5], ['Google Scholar', 'snowball', 'search'])\ngrab([10], ['Self Consistency', 'majority'])\ngrab([23], ['Toolformer', 'calendar', 'ToolBench'])\n```","reasoning_content":"I have all five notes. Now merge into report.json. Need to read report.json first (registered full read already). Need exact quotes. I have quotes from delivered evidence pages 13, 45, 52. But I need quotes for other answers: categories (page 4/5), self_consistency (page 10), toolformer (page 23), CAMEL (page 45), generative agents evaluators (page 47), Table 4 (page 51). My notes contain quotes but I need continuous exact original text. Risky. I should read pages 4, 5, 10, 23, 45, 47, 51 to get exact quotes. But request budget: requests_left=6? \"requests_after_response\":6. Careful. I need to be efficient.\n\nActually reading pages costs model requests too? Each action is a request. I have 6 requests after this response apparently. Let me batch: one read of pages 4-5, 10, 23, 45, 47, 51 in one action (multiple read_pdf calls in one block, that's one request). But output may be truncated: The delivery shows full text of pages 13, 45, 52 which were long.